# Docker build context ignore rules.
#
# NOTE ON SCOPE: the bot services (teams-bot, feishu-bot) are built with the
# REPOSITORY ROOT as their context, because they depend on the sibling package
# im-core/ and a per-service context cannot see it. Docker only ever reads a
# .dockerignore that sits at the context root, which is why this file exists
# instead of the per-service ones that used to live in teams-bot/.
#
# Keep this list to things no Dockerfile needs. Do not exclude whole service
# directories: the Dockerfiles COPY from im-core/, teams-bot/ and feishu-bot/.

# Version control & docs
.git/
.gitignore
**/*.md
!README.md

# Python artifacts (dev virtualenvs are per-package and large)
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
.python-version

# Node artifacts (web_ui is built by its own Dockerfile under web_ui/)
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/.turbo/

# Local env & secrets — never ship these into an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor / OS noise
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
